p.src:
Each tensor index transforms independently. For a tensor with two lower indices, $T_{mr}^{(y)}
  =
  \frac{\partial x^{n}}{\partial y^{m}}
  \frac{\partial x^{s}}{\partial y^{r}}
  T_{ns}^{(x)}.$ For one upper and one lower index, $\bigl(T^{m}{}_{r}\bigr)_{(y)}
  =
  \frac{\partial y^{m}}{\partial x^{n}}
  \frac{\partial x^{s}}{\partial y^{r}}
  \bigl(T^{n}{}_{s}\bigr)_{(x)}.$ The general rule is one direct Jacobian for every upper index and one inverse Jacobian for every lower index.

