p.src:
To prove that $g_{mn}$ is a tensor, rewrite the same scalar in the $y$-coordinates: $dx^{m}
  =
  \frac{\partial x^{m}}{\partial y^{r}}\,dy^{r}.$ Substitution gives $\begin{aligned}
  ds^{2}
  &=
  g_{mn}^{(x)}
  \frac{\partial x^{m}}{\partial y^{r}}
  \frac{\partial x^{n}}{\partial y^{s}}
  dy^{r}dy^{s}
  \nonumber\\
  &=
  g_{rs}^{(y)}\,dy^{r}dy^{s},
  \end{aligned}$ and therefore $\boxed{
  g_{rs}^{(y)}
  =
  \frac{\partial x^{m}}{\partial y^{r}}
  \frac{\partial x^{n}}{\partial y^{s}}
  g_{mn}^{(x)}.}$ This is exactly the covariant rank-two law.

