p.src:
In polar coordinates on the plane, $ds^{2}=dr^{2}+r^{2}d\theta^{2},$ so $(g_{mn})
  =
  \begin{pmatrix}
    1&0\\
    0&r^{2}
  \end{pmatrix},
  \qquad
  (g^{mn})
  =
  \begin{pmatrix}
    1&0\\
    0&r^{-2}
  \end{pmatrix}.$ For a diagonal matrix, inversion simply reciprocates each diagonal entry.

