Only the symmetric part contributes to the quadratic form. Indeed, $g_{12}\,dx^{1}dx^{2}
  +
  g_{21}\,dx^{2}dx^{1}
  =
  (g_{12}+g_{21})\,dx^{1}dx^{2}.$ An antisymmetric part would cancel because the coordinate differentials commute.

