p.src:
Spacetime has one time coordinate and three spatial coordinates. In one space dimension, a Euclidean-looking sum $dt^{2}+dx^{2}$ is not preserved by Lorentz transformations. The invariant quantity is the proper-time interval $\boxed{
  d\tau^{2}
  =
  dt^{2}-dx^{2}}
  \qquad (c=1).$

