p.src:
Setting $c=1$ makes time and distance use the same unit. Keeping different units would be like measuring one Cartesian direction in feet and another in inches: conversion factors would obscure the geometric symmetry. If $c$ is restored, $d\tau^{2}
  =
  dt^{2}-\frac{dx^{2}}{c^{2}},$ when $d\tau$ is measured in time units.

