p.src:
Accelerated coordinates have already shown that curvilinear coordinates are useful in spacetime even before genuine gravitational curvature is introduced. Write $x^{\mu}=(x^{0},x^{1},x^{2},x^{3}),
  \qquad
  x^{0}=t.$ Greek indices run over spacetime coordinates. In arbitrary coordinates the proper-time element takes the tensorial form $\boxed{
  d\tau^{2}
  =
  g_{\mu\nu}(x)\,dx^{\mu}dx^{\nu}.}$

