p.src:
In Minkowski coordinates, $\eta_{\mu\nu}
  =
  \operatorname{diag}(1,-1,-1,-1),$ and $d\tau^{2}
  =
  \eta_{\mu\nu}\,dx^{\mu}dx^{\nu}.$ The symbol $\eta_{\mu\nu}$ is the spacetime counterpart of the Cartesian $\delta_{mn}$, but its signs encode a Lorentzian rather than Euclidean geometry.

